StrideGP

Pedestrian inertial navigation in Julia: a ZUPT-aided (zero-velocity update) strapdown
INS whose stride increments are corrected online by a Hilbert-space Gaussian process
(HSGP) learned from mocap/reference ground truth, with the stride model's coefficients
estimated inside the filter.

Running (from the repository root, Julia 1.12):

    julia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'
    julia --project=. scripts/4OnlineCorrection/4_hybrid_zupt_ins.jl
    julia --project=. -t 1 -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.test()'

Scripts load the package with `using StrideGP`; the figure scripts in scripts/5Results/
share scripts/5Results/_common.jl. Data is expected under data/ and outputs go to out/
(both gitignored).

Thank you for the HSGP hyperparameter optimization code and HSGP basis function code from
Kok, M., Solin, A., & Schön, T. B. (2024). Rao-Blackwellized Particle Smoothing for
Simultaneous Localization and Mapping. Data-Centric Engineering, 5.
https://doi.org/10.1017/dce.2024.12
